Computational Complexity and Efficiency Analysis
================================================

Let

N = number of snapshots
P = number of particles per snapshot

These movies operate ONLY on already-computed time series
(j_spec_matrix and spin_param), meaning the expensive particle
computations have already been completed earlier.

------------------------------------------------
1. Time Complexity
------------------------------------------------

Angular Momentum Vector Movie

Per frame operations:

• Clear axes
• Plot trajectory of length i
• Plot current point

Time per frame: O(i)

Total runtime:

Σ(i=1→N) O(i) = O(N²)

With N ≈ 800 snapshots:

N² ≈ 640,000 operations

This is trivial for modern CPUs.


Spin Parameter Movie

Per frame:

• plot array of length i

Time per frame: O(i)

Total runtime:

O(N²)

Again extremely small computational cost.


------------------------------------------------
2. Space Complexity
------------------------------------------------

Memory requirements are minimal.

j_spec_matrix

size = N × 3

For N = 800

Memory ≈ 800 × 3 × 8 bytes
       ≈ 19 KB

spin_param

size = N

Memory ≈ 800 × 8 bytes
       ≈ 6 KB

Total memory footprint is far below 1 MB.


------------------------------------------------
3. Movie Encoding Cost
------------------------------------------------

Most runtime is dominated by:

• matplotlib rendering
• FFmpeg encoding

Frame generation complexity:

O(N_frames)

With fps = 20 and 800 frames:

movie length ≈ 40 seconds


------------------------------------------------
4. Why This Is Computationally Efficient
------------------------------------------------

The expensive operations in the pipeline are:

• particle loading
• angular momentum calculation
• inertia tensor calculation
• convex hull construction

Those scale roughly:

O(P) or O(P log P)

where P ≈ millions of particles.

These movie modules avoid recomputing any particle physics.

They only visualize precomputed quantities, meaning the
visualization layer is extremely lightweight.


------------------------------------------------
5. Scientific Interpretation
------------------------------------------------

Angular Momentum Vector Movie reveals:

• orbital torque phases
• spin flips
• angular momentum transfer during merger
• final spin alignment


Spin Parameter Movie reveals:

• halo spin growth
• merger-driven angular momentum injection
• post-merger relaxation


Together they provide a dynamical view of how the MW–M31
merger redistributes angular momentum in the combined halo.
